discussions.body:
**Package:** `@deepseek-ai/dsh` 0.1.2-rc.1 / `@deepseek-ai/dsh-subprocess-local` ^0.1.2-rc.1 (line numbers below refer to the bundled `lib/index.js` in the published package)
**Environment:** Windows 11, Node v22.17.0
**Severity:** critical — a single deleted `%TEMP%` directory terminates the entire `dsh web` server and every live session

## Summary

`OutputCollector.spillAll()` in `dsh-subprocess-local` calls `openSync()`/`writeSync()` with no error handling, synchronously inside a stream `data` handler. The collector's spill directory is created **once per process** (`%TEMP%\dsh-subprocess-<random>`, via `mkdtempSync`) and can never be recreated. When something deletes that directory mid-session — a temp cleaner, antivirus, or manual sweep — the first subprocess whose output exceeds the in-memory cap throws an uncaught `ENOENT` that kills the whole `dsh web` process, not just the affected subprocess.

Observed in the wild: a `dsh web` instance ~83 minutes into its run died exactly this way on its *first-ever* spill (the generated file name's spill counter was `-1-`).

## Stack (verbatim)

```
Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory, open 'C:\Users\Prime\AppData\Local\Temp\dsh-subprocess-Kp72eM\dsh-subprocess-18596-1-8ee8c7f6420e-stdout.log'
    at openSync (node:fs:561:18)
    at OutputCollector.spillAll (file:///C:/Users/Prime/AppData/Local/npm-cache/_npx/1e7f6d9597241db0/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-subprocess-local/lib/index.js:717:19)
    at OutputCollector.push (file:///C:/Users/Prime/AppData/Local/npm-cache/_npx/1e7f6d9597241db0/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-subprocess-local/lib/index.js:693:75)
    at Socket.<anonymous> (file:///C:/Users/Prime/AppData/Local/npm-cache/_npx/1e7f6d9597241db0/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-subprocess-local/lib/index.js:862:14)
    at Socket.emit (node:events:518:28)
    at addChunk (node:internal/streams/readable:561:12)
    ...
Node.js v22.17.0
```

## Root cause

- `lib/index.js:648-651` — spill dir created once per process via `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), "dsh-subprocess-"))` and cached in `defaultSpillDir`. The module imports no `mkdir`, so it can never be recreated.
- `lib/index.js:710-721` — `spillAll()` performs `openSync(this.spillFile, "wx", 384)` and `writeSync(...)` with **no try/catch**, synchronously inside the child stream's `data` handler (`push()` at `:693`, wired at `:862`). Any failure escapes as an uncaught exception and terminates the entire server.
- Nothing in the `@deepseek-ai/*` packages ever deletes these dirs (a source-wide search finds only the `mkdtemp` line, the per-file name template, and dependency pins), so an external `%TEMP%` sweep of a *live* dir guarantees this crash on the next spill.
- Adjacent: stale `dsh-subprocess-*` dirs are never pruned — six accumulated over ten days of normal use on the reporting machine.

## Repro

1. `npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web`, open a session (the spill dir is created lazily when the first spill-capped subprocess spawns).
2. Delete `%TEMP%\dsh-subprocess-*` while the server runs.
3. Produce subprocess output exceeding the in-memory collection cap (e.g. a chatty session agent or MCP child stdout). The whole server exits with the stack above.

## Suggested fix (applied and verified locally)

Wrap the spill path in try/catch; on failure degrade to the existing tail-only path via `discardSpill()` (which already sets `spillDisabled = true`), recreate the dir on `ENOENT` so later collectors can spill again, and warn once per process. Add `mkdirSync` to the `node:fs` import.

```diff
--- a/lib/index.js
+++ b/lib/index.js
@@ import
-import { closeSync, constants, mkdtempSync, openSync, readFileSync, readSync, readdirSync, readlinkSync, statSync, unlinkSync, writeSync } from "node:fs";
+import { closeSync, constants, mkdirSync, mkdtempSync, openSync, readFileSync, readSync, readdirSync, readlinkSync, statSync, unlinkSync, writeSync } from "node:fs";
@@ spillAll
 	spillAll(chunk) {
 		if (this.maxSpillBytes !== void 0 && this.total > this.maxSpillBytes) {
 			this.discardSpill();
 			return;
 		}
-		if (this.spillFd === void 0) {
-			this.spillFile = join(this.spillDir, `dsh-subprocess-${process.pid}-${++spillCounter}-${randomBytes(6).toString("hex")}-${this.label}.log`);
-			this.spillFd = openSync(this.spillFile, "wx", 384);
-			for (const prior of this.chunks) writeSync(this.spillFd, prior);
-		}
-		writeSync(this.spillFd, chunk);
+		try {
+			if (this.spillFd === void 0) {
+				this.spillFile = join(this.spillDir, `dsh-subprocess-${process.pid}-${++spillCounter}-${randomBytes(6).toString("hex")}-${this.label}.log`);
+				this.spillFd = openSync(this.spillFile, "wx", 384);
+				for (const prior of this.chunks) writeSync(this.spillFd, prior);
+			}
+			writeSync(this.spillFd, chunk);
+		} catch (error) {
+			this.discardSpill();
+			if (error?.code === "ENOENT") {
+				try { mkdirSync(this.spillDir, { recursive: true }); } catch {}
+			}
+			if (OutputCollector._spillWarned !== true) {
+				OutputCollector._spillWarned = true;
+				console.warn(`dsh-subprocess-local: output spill to ${this.spillDir} failed (${error?.code ?? error?.message ?? String(error)}); degraded to in-memory tail${error?.code === "ENOENT" ? " and recreated the spill dir" : ""}`);
+			}
+		}
 	}
```

Optional hardening: prune stale `dsh-subprocess-*` dirs at startup (they currently leak forever), and consider a process-level `uncaughtException` guard for the web server so one subsystem cannot terminate every session.

## Summary

In the user message bubble, a long pasted URL / `@file` reference is rendered as a `nowrap` chip (`projectUserText` → `.refChip`). The chip cannot wrap, so the bubble expands past the chat column and the rest of the viewport.

This is stock chat rendering in `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-primitives` + `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-chat`, not a plugin.

## Reproduction

1. Open DSH Desktop / `dsh web`.
2. Paste a message that contains a long Figma (or similar) URL, e.g.

   ```
   Implement this design from Figma.
   https://www.figma.com/design/...?node-id=...
   ```

   The URL may also be projected as an `@…` reference chip (percent-encoded Chinese path, no spaces).
3. Send the message.

## Current behavior

- The user bubble grows horizontally with the chip.
- The transcript overflows the screen; later text in the same bubble is pushed off-canvas.
- `.UQgv6G_bubble` already has `word-break: break-word`, but `.refChip { white-space: nowrap }` (and previously `inline-flex`) wins for the chip.

Relevant source (current master):

```css
/* packages/client/ui-primitives/src/user-text.module.css */
.refChip {
  display: inline;
  margin: 0 2px;
  color: var(--dsw-alias-state-business-primary);
  font-weight: 500;
  white-space: nowrap;
}
```

`projectUserText` treats `/path` and `@token` runs as chips (`packages/client/ui-primitives`). User bubbles consume that projection in `UserStyleBubble` (`packages/client/ui-chat`).

## Expected behavior

Long chips wrap inside the bubble (`max-width: 100%` of `.userStack`). The bubble stays within `max-width: min(calc(var(--dsh-chat-content-width, 748px) * .702), 82%)`. Hover `title` can still show the full token.

Suggested CSS (queue preview already uses nowrap/ellipsis on the consumer; this only needs to apply in the wrapping bubble):

```css
.refChip {
  display: inline;
  max-width: 100%;
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  white-space: normal; /* or: wrap inside bubble, keep nowrap+ellipsis in the queue preview */
}
```

If `nowrap` must stay for short `@file` chips, wrap only when the token has no natural break points (URLs / percent-encoded paths), or let the bubble consumer override:

```css
.UQgv6G_bubble [data-ref-chip] {
  white-space: normal;
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  word-break: break-all;
}
```

## Environment

- DSH Desktop 2.0.4 (GUI `http://127.0.0.1:43120`)
- `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-primitives@0.1.2-rc.1`
- macOS

## 问题

模型输出的工具调用参数里，超出 `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` 的大整数（如各类业务 ID）在 `JSON.parse` 后精度丢失。

使用 **Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-FP8** 可稳定复现该问题。

复现：给模型的输入包含

```
用户 ID: 900719925474099123
订单 ID: 1234567890123456789
类别 ID: b3f1c9d24e7a4f0e9c1a2b3c4d5e6f70
```

模型输出：

```json
{
  "user_id": 900719925474099123,
  "order_id": 1234567890123456789,
  "category_id": "b3f1c9d24e7a4f0e9c1a2b3c4d5e6f70"
}
```

`parseArguments` 里 `JSON.parse` 之后变成 `900719925474099100`、`1234567890123456800`，最终下发到请求头/参数即为错误值。

## 原因

`packages/core/agent-loop/src/tool-calls.ts` 的 `parseArguments` 直接 `JSON.parse(raw)`，19 位整数被双精度浮点表示后四舍五入；另外模型把声明为 `string` 的 ID 字段写成数字时，也没有按 schema 还原类型。

## 修复

### 1. `packages/core/agent-loop/src/tool-calls.ts`

`parseArguments` 改为接收工具声明的 `parameters` schema，先给超限整数字面量加引号再解析，随后按 schema 强转类型：

```ts
/**
 * Parse model arguments against the tool's declared parameter schema,
 * preserving invalid JSON as text and mapping empty input to `{}`. Integer
 * literals beyond the safe-integer range survive verbatim, and numeric values
 * are coerced to the string form their field declares.
 */
function parseArguments(raw: string, parameters: Record<string, unknown> | undefined): unknown {
  if (!raw) return {}
  try {
    return coerceToSchema(JSON.parse(quoteUnsafeIntegers(raw)), parameters)
  } catch {
    return raw
  }
}

/** Matches one JSON string literal or number token, in order of appearance. */
const JSON_STRING_OR_NUMBER = /"(?:[^"\\]|\\.)*"|-?(?:0|[1-9]\d*)(?:\.\d+)?(?:[eE][+-]?\d+)?/g

/** The largest magnitude every double represents as an exact integer, as digits. */
const MAX_SAFE_INTEGER_DIGITS = String(Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER)

/**
 * Quote integer literals beyond the safe-integer range before `JSON.parse`
 * rounds them, so their digits survive verbatim (e.g. a 19-digit tenant id).
 */
function quoteUnsafeIntegers(raw: string): string {
  let out = ''
  let last = 0
  let match: RegExpExecArray | null
  while ((match = JSON_STRING_OR_NUMBER.exec(raw)) !== null) {
    const token = match[0]
    out += raw.slice(last, match.index)
    if (!token.startsWith('"') && isUnsafeIntegerLiteral(token)) out += `"${token}"`
    else out += token
    last = match.index + token.length
  }
  return out + raw.slice(last)
}

/** Whether an integer literal's magnitude exceeds the safe-integer range. */
function isUnsafeIntegerLiteral(token: string): boolean {
  const digits = token.startsWith('-') ? token.slice(1) : token
  return digits.length > MAX_SAFE_INTEGER_DIGITS.length
    || (digits.length === MAX_SAFE_INTEGER_DIGITS.length && digits > MAX_SAFE_INTEGER_DIGITS)
}

/**
 * Coerce parsed values toward the tool's declared parameter types: a
 * `string`-typed field receives the string form of a numeric value, so an id
 * the model emitted as a number keeps its declared type.
 */
function coerceToSchema(value: unknown, schema: Record<string, unknown> | undefined): unknown {
  if (schema === undefined) return value
  if (schema.type === 'string' && typeof value === 'number') return String(value)
  if (Array.isArray(value)) {
    const items = schema.items
    return items === undefined ? value : value.map(item => coerceToSchema(item, items as Record<string, unknown>))
  }
  if (typeof value === 'object' && value !== null) {
    const record = value as Record<string, unknown>
    const properties = schema.properties
    if (properties !== undefined) {
      for (const key of Object.keys(record)) {
        const child = (properties as Record<string, unknown>)[key]
        if (child !== undefined) record[key] = coerceToSchema(record[key], child as Record<string, unknown>)
      }
    }
    return record
  }
  return value
}
```

调用点同步传入 schema：

```diff
-      arguments: parseArguments(block.arguments),
+      arguments: parseArguments(block.arguments, ctx.tools.get(block.name)?.parameters),
```

