我们在排查 CLI 退出延迟时，发现正常退出路径可能存在一个超时保护缺口。这里提供复现方式和一个较小的修复建议，供维护者参考。

### 问题描述

在 `apps/cli/src/process-shutdown.ts` 中，正常调用 `shutdown()` 且应用清理成功后，`completeOnce()` 会：

1. 清除五秒退出定时器；
2. 设置 `process.exitCode`；
3. 等待 Node 自然退出。

如果此时仍有原生句柄存活，例如原生 WebSocket 已调用 `close()`，但远端始终没有回应关闭握手，进程就可能继续等待。由于兜底定时器已经取消，这段等待不再受 CLI 原有五秒期限保护。

检查的源码版本为：

- `dsh-v0.1.5-alpha.1`
- 提交：`5dda764ed3aa172535a7967b06ff95d9cbfe536a`
- [[对应源码](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/blob/5dda764ed3aa172535a7967b06ff95d9cbfe536a/apps/cli/src/process-shutdown.ts)](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/blob/5dda764ed3aa172535a7967b06ff95d9cbfe536a/apps/cli/src/process-shutdown.ts)

### 最小复现

环境：macOS、Node.js `v26.7.0`。不需要真实账号或外部服务。

在上述版本的源码仓库根目录执行以下命令。本地服务会接受 WebSocket 连接，但故意不回应关闭握手；服务端句柄均调用 `unref()`，避免服务端本身影响进程退出判断。

```bash
node --input-type=module <<'JS'
import { createServer } from 'node:http';
import { createHash } from 'node:crypto';
import { createProcessShutdown } from './apps/cli/src/process-shutdown.ts';

const server = createServer();

server.on('upgrade', (request, socket) => {
  const accept = createHash('sha1')
    .update(
      request.headers['sec-websocket-key'] +
      '258EAFA5-E914-47DA-95CA-C5AB0DC85B11'
    )
    .digest('base64');

  socket.write(
    'HTTP/1.1 101 Switching Protocols\r\n' +
    'Upgrade: websocket\r\n' +
    'Connection: Upgrade\r\n' +
    `Sec-WebSocket-Accept: ${accept}\r\n\r\n`
  );

  socket.on('data', () => {});
  socket.unref();
});

await new Promise(resolve => server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', resolve));
server.unref();

const socket = new WebSocket(`ws://127.0.0.1:${server.address().port}`);

await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
  socket.addEventListener('open', resolve);
  socket.addEventListener('error', reject);
});

await createProcessShutdown(async () => {
  socket.close();
  console.log('Application disposal completed');
}).shutdown(0);
JS
```

**预期行为：** 清理成功后允许 Node 自然退出；如果仍有句柄阻止退出，原有五秒期限继续生效。

**实际行为：** 输出 `Application disposal completed` 后，进程仍然存活。本地测试观察到清理完成后约 6.46 秒仍未退出，随后由测试程序终止。这说明等待已超过原有五秒期限，但该测试没有测量最终自然退出所需时间。

### 修复建议

正常清理成功后，将兜底定时器设为不持有引用，而不是取消：

```diff
 const completeOnce = (code: number): void => {
   if (completed || forceExited) return;
   completed = true;
-  clearExitTimeout();
+  timeout?.unref();
   complete(code);
 };
```

这样可以同时保留两种行为：

- **没有残留句柄：** 定时器不会阻止 Node 自然退出，不必等待五秒。
- **仍有残留句柄：** 定时器继续生效，到达从关闭开始计算的原有期限时执行强制退出。

这项修改不延长或重新计算截止时间，也不改变退出码、清理失败处理及信号升级逻辑。

我们注意到 [[此前的修复](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/commit/4619f183ff297c7ec42b6c26cd0fee2a5a08c374)](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/commit/4619f183ff297c7ec42b6c26cd0fee2a5a08c374) 为规避 Windows 原生句柄断言问题，刻意避免在正常清理后立即调用 `process.exit()`。上述方案保留这一设计，只让原有超时保护覆盖清理后的句柄排空阶段。

### 本地验证

已准备以下回归测试：

- 清理完成后，剩余句柄等待仍受原有期限约束；
- 没有残留句柄时，子进程无需等待截止时间即可自然退出；
- 原生 WebSocket 对端不回应关闭握手时，子进程仍能按期限退出。

未修改的上游代码会失败其中两项新增回归；应用补丁后，12 项相关测试全部通过。局部严格 TypeScript 检查、仓库 oxlint、相关文档配对及 Agent Note 格式检查也已通过。

## Environment

- DSH `0.1.5-alpha.1» (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-conversation@0.1.5-alpha.1», npm `alpha» dist-tag, published 2026-09-08)
- Windows 11 · Microsoft Edge (also reproduced on Chrome) · Microsoft Pinyin IME
- Bundled Lexical `0.49.0»

## Summary

In the Web composer, typing **after a claimed slash-command token** (e.g. `/plan» followed by text) intermittently:

1. renders the newly typed text in the claim color (amber) instead of the normal text color;
2. drops/loses the characters just typed; and/or
3. throws `Minified Lexical error #14» from the composer's `onError: (error) => { throw error }», leaving the composer broken until a page refresh.

Screenshot — the seat where it happens (claimed `/plan» token in amber, followed by typed text):

![DSH Web composer: claimed /plan token followed by typed text](https://gist.github.com/kaijia323/404c0289bb4ea82a3dfdbe054c998424/raw/dsh-composer-claim-seat.png)

*The screenshot shows the normal state; in the faulty runs the text after `/plan» also turns amber, or disappears.*

## Steps to reproduce

1. Open any session in the Web GUI and focus the composer.
2. Type `/plan» and let the command claim settle — the token turns amber. Do **not** press Enter.
3. Keep typing after the token (Chinese via Microsoft Pinyin, e.g. `暗色的阿松大», or simply extra characters).
4. Intermittently the new text turns amber, or vanishes; sometimes the composer throws error #14.

## Observed error

```text
Uncaught Error: Minified Lexical error #14; visit https://lexical.dev/docs/error?code=14 for the full message or use the non-minified dev environment for full errors and additional helpful warnings.
    at t (client.js:3303:1)
    at di (client.js:7232:1)
    at Js (client.js:8745:1)
    at Wo.getWritable (client.js:5343:1)
    at Wo.setTextContent (client.js:5786:1)
    at Wo.mergeWithSibling (client.js:5891:1)
    at Ft$1 (client.js:3879:1)
    at Pt$1 (client.js:3898:1)
    at client.js:7533:1
    at Mi (client.js:7550:1)
```

Frame mapping (against `dsh-client-ui-conversation/lib/client.js» + `lexical@0.49.0»):

| frame | function |
| --- | --- |
| `t» | `invariant» |
| `di» | `errorOnInfiniteTransforms» — `infiniteTransformCount > 99 && invariant(false)» |
| `Js» | node-write dirty marking |
| `Wo.*» | `TextNode.getWritable» / `setTextContent» / `mergeWithSibling» |
| `Ft$1» | `$mergeWithSibling» |
| `Pt$1» | `$normalizeTextNode» |
| `client.js:7533» / `Mi» | dirty-leaf reconciliation loop |

Note: **#14 is the "transforms endlessly triggering additional transforms" guard**, not "Unable to find an active editor state" (that is #195 in the same build).

## Root cause

`packages/client/ui-conversation/src/client/input/editor/claim-decor.ts» (`registerClaimDecoration», introduced with the Lexical composer rewrite `b519cb87»), lines 43-47:

```ts
if (text.length > token.length) {
  // Typing at the token boundary lands in the styled node; split the
  // overflow back out so only the token itself carries the color.
  const [tokenNode] = node.splitText(token.length)
  if (tokenNode !== undefined && tokenNode.getStyle() !== TOKEN_STYLE) tokenNode.setStyle(TOKEN_STYLE)
  return
}
```

`TextNode.splitText» copies `style» to every part (`lexical/src/nodes/LexicalTextNode.ts:1017-1019» reads `style» once; `:1040-1052» applies it to each part). When the token leaf is **already** styled with `TOKEN_STYLE» and then gains trailing text — the normal incremental-typing path — both halves keep `TOKEN_STYLE». `$normalizeTextNode» sees equal `mode»/`format»/`style» and merges them back into one styled node; the transform splits again on the next pass; after 100 reconciliation passes Lexical throws #14.

Which symptom appears depends on dirty-leaf processing order:

- overflow transform runs first → it hits the "off the token seat" branch and clears its style → converges, text stays black;
- first-leaf normalization runs first → merge → amber overflow text and/or #14;
- an aborted commit loses the characters typed in that update.

Chinese IME makes it frequent and intermittent because composition updates repeatedly replace the same text node, flipping the dirty-leaf order from keystroke to keystroke.

The existing test `packages/client/ui-conversation/tests/lexical-editor-core.client.spec.tsx:428-465» inserts `/plan rest» in a single update (leaf starts unstyled, so it splits once and converges). It never exercises the incremental path (style first, then append), which is why this slipped through.

## Minimal headless repro (no DSH needed)

Run with `lexical@0.49.0»; it reproduces the exact 10-frame stack:

```js
// node repro-lexical-14.cjs   (requires lexical@0.49.0)
const L = require('lexical/dist/Lexical.prod.js');
const TOKEN = '/plan';
const STYLE = 'color: var(--dsw-alias-state-warn-label)';

const firstTextLeaf = () => {
  const block = L.$getRoot().getFirstChild();
  const leaf = L.$isElementNode(block) ? block.getFirstChild() : null;
  return L.$isTextNode(leaf) ? leaf : null;
};

const editor = L.createEditor({ namespace: 'repro' });
editor.registerNodeTransform(L.TextNode, (node) => {
  const first = firstTextLeaf();
  if (first === null || node.getKey() !== first.getKey()) {
    if (node.getStyle() === STYLE) node.setStyle('');
    return;
  }
  const text = node.getTextContent();
  if (!text.startsWith(TOKEN)) {
    if (node.getStyle() === STYLE) node.setStyle('');
    return;
  }
  if (text.length > TOKEN.length) {
    const [tokenNode] = node.splitText(TOKEN.length);
    if (tokenNode !== undefined && tokenNode.getStyle() !== STYLE) tokenNode.setStyle(STYLE);
    return;
  }
  if (node.getStyle() !== STYLE) node.setStyle(STYLE);
});

// 1) type the token — the claim decoration styles it amber
editor.update(() => {
  const p = L.$createParagraphNode();
  p.append(L.$createTextNode(TOKEN));
  L.$getRoot().append(p);
}, { discrete: true });

// 2) type one more character at the token boundary -> Minified Lexical error #14
editor.update(() => {
  firstTextLeaf().setTextContent(TOKEN + 'x');
}, { discrete: true });
```

Result: `Minified Lexical error #14» with `t → Ur → li → getWritable → setTextContent → mergeWithSibling → St → Tt → anon → ss» — the same shape as the shipped stack.

## Proposed fix

Make the overflow segment drop `TOKEN_STYLE» after the split, so normalization cannot re-merge the halves:

```ts
if (text.length > token.length) {
  const [tokenNode, overflow] = node.splitText(token.length)
  if (tokenNode !== undefined && tokenNode.getStyle() !== TOKEN_STYLE) tokenNode.setStyle(TOKEN_STYLE)
  if (overflow !== undefined && overflow.getStyle() === TOKEN_STYLE) overflow.setStyle('')
  return
}
```

A regression test should drive the incremental path (create the claimed token, then insert one character) and assert: token amber, overflow unstyled, no #14.

